@group CCO full set (`@modset cc_only full`, was `cc_only_srv.sh OUT LEVEL full`)
@commands rerun SQ-CCO-08 with entity data: in the End `summon zombie 0 70 0 {NoAI:1b,PersistenceRequired:1b}`, `summon villager 5 70 0 {NoAI:1b}`, join a survival bot or player; `data get entity @e[type=zombie,limit=1] Attributes` and the same for the villager; `execute as @e[type=zombie,limit=1] at @s if biome ~ ~ ~ #minecraft:is_end run say IN_END`; do it with `gravityLimitDimensions` true, then `qrun.py toml srv/config/creativecommon-common.toml perf gravityLimitDimensions false` and reboot; also SQ-CGE-02 on this set
@pass the zombie, villager and survivor each carry `forge:entity_gravity` with a modifier named "Low Gravity Biome" (-0.8) while IN_END prints; falling blocks as SQ-CGE-02. If the modifier is missing while IN_END prints: record the `biome_configs` the set wrote, `cache_time`, and `grep -i "gravity" logs/latest.log` (the finding for TODO `creativecommon/publish #3`; Common is not at fault unless it also fails with the mixin config switched off)
@fails Create Gravity `ServerConfig.reloadConfig` timing (server started before tags), the entity's `fallFlying` / blacklist tag, then Common's gate
@from batches/r1108cge/b5_cco.qb
@modset cc_only full
> difficulty normal
> execute in minecraft:the_end run forceload add 0 0
> pbot spawn cge06 0 75 0 minecraft:the_end survival
sleep 3
> zgv cfg the_end 0 70 0
waitlog \[zgv\] cfg dim=minecraft:the_end 10
> execute in minecraft:the_end run summon minecraft:zombie 0 75 0 {NoAI:1b,PersistenceRequired:1b,Tags:["cge06"]}
> execute in minecraft:the_end run summon minecraft:villager 5 75 0 {NoAI:1b,PersistenceRequired:1b,Tags:["cge06"]}
sleep 6
